<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92452" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥικν-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>shrivelled with cold</i>,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεφρικώς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				1091
			</span></i>; <i>shrivelled</i> by old age or disease, <i>shrunk,
				contracted</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Prog.</u>
				2
			</span></i> (s. v.l.), <i><span class="en">
				Xenarch.
				4.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cerc.
				2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				49
			</span></i>, etc.: generally, <i>withered, shrivelled, crooked</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἥφαιστος ῥικνὸς πόδας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Ap.</u>
					317
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅψεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>C.</u>
					2.346
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥικνοὶ πόδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.669
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>APl.</u>
				4.306
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥ. καὶ κώδιον</span>
			<i>shrivelled</i> and (like) leather, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				14.1363.15
			</span></i> (Rome, <span class="entity">iv A.D.</span>).</div>
